  "clinical_note": "v1.1 normalization-skew fix. Same Ghana-priors simulator cohort as v1.0 (4 citation groups), but the distilled MLP is trained and served on the [0,1] SCHEMA_NORM representation - the exact tensor the app feeds at inference. v1.0 distilled from RAW feature scales, so its input quantization clamped every app input to ~0 (train/serve skew); v1.1's flatbuffer input quantization covers [0,1] (scale=0.003922, zero_point=-128). Calibration via Platt scaling on the internal 20% hold-out; 95% CI from per-bin Platt-residual std; drift detection via per-feature z-score against the normalized training distribution.",
